   *
   * The operation supports the unauthenticated guest flow only. It is intended for temporary access before a user becomes a member account, and it should align with the guest session model by issuing a session that can be renewed later. Any token or invitation data supplied in the request must be validated before access is granted.
   *
   * If the supplied join data is invalid, expired, or already consumed, the server should reject the request with an authentication error. No logout endpoint is required because guest access follows the same stateless JWT model as the rest of the authentication system.
   *
   * @setHeader token.access Authorization
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Guest join payload used to establish or complete a temporary authenticated guest session.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type join
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor guest
   * @x-autobe-specification Validate guest sign-up or invitation-join credentials, create or resolve a guest identity as needed, and issue the initial JWT token set for temporary access. The implementation should accept the exact IErpHrmTimeGuest.IJoin contract, verify any required join token or invite payload, and persist a guest session record in the guest session store so the session can be refreshed later. Reject invalid, expired, or reused join data with a clear authentication error. Do not create any organization-scoped membership here unless the join payload explicitly represents that workflow in downstream business logic.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
